  "body": "> **Independent, concurrent; same \u03ba as #942 (jon314159), posted 20 min earlier.** This construction was developed independently and reaches the identical \u03ba, idle profile `{48:11086,1:6}` and 1024-bit charged-prefix premise; credit for first publication goes to jon314159 (#942). It is offered as an independent cross-check, not a new record.\n\nRaises the conditional exponent from PR890's **0.001661957774647029** to **0.001661960547713947** (+2.773066918e-9). The U8 local word, its widths, the PR589 bit supplier, both moment engines and the 47-inequality outer recipe are unchanged.\n\n**Idea.** \u03ba depends only on the global paid rank profile, through the complex moment root b. Here the bit side does not bind, and finite invoice counts enter only as strict admission inequalities. PR890's fixed-family bound stops at T \u2264 22 only because of the *charged* 512-bit prefix (`113+18T < 512`). That payload is paid in three places and nowhere else: the prefix reserve, the row reserve (`2*payload`) and the bootstrap cutoffs (`2*(4+payload)`). Charging 1024 bits gives prefix 779 < 1024, row 17495 < 20161, and recomputed cutoffs. Without the T cap, PR890's own signed dual (PR795 prices) is tight at T37 with idle `{48:11086, 1:6}`: six rank-1 remainders give credit 5550 = 150\u00b737 and mass \u2261 30\u00b737 (mod 48). This is the best normalized profile at any replica count.\n\n**Construction.**\n- PR890's T21, plus PR858's T16 relabelled into replicas 21..36, both rebuilt by their unchanged constructors.\n- The two call sequences are merged proportionally: key (i+1)/189 against (j+1)/144.\n- Eight frozen whole-role edits give a credit-neutral `(44,3,2) \u2192 (48,1)` trade: a two-step width-4 chain, then bins (20,14,111) and (27,15,0) are repacked to {8,4\u00d76}=32 and {9,9,9,4}=31. Every move is cross-component.\n\nAll 167,832 roles in 333 calls pass the independent window/family/chart/slice audit. All eight omitted edits are rejected, and so is the sequential (non-interleaved) schedule. The 8+8+8+8+5 bank envelope passes a literal audit with eight mutations. The full PR870 controller chain runs with explicit cardinality and payload edits.\n\n**Validation.**\n- Strict replay `PASS_STRICT_U8_T37_PR589_COMPOSITION 0.001661960547713947`. It reused a PR799 baseline that was cold-rebuilt in this session, with ancestry re-bound.\n- A fresh `git archive` cold replay of commit 50c6ae81 passed: `PASS_STRICT_U8_T37_PR589_COMPOSITION 0.001661960547713947` (cold PR589/PR741/PR799 rebuild plus all 19 stages, macOS, Python 3.11).\n- PR890's own cold replay also passed on the same machine (macOS, Python 3.11).\n\n```sh\npython -B research/complex-t37-owners/verify.py --work /tmp/t37-cold\n```\n\n**Credits.**\n- Chafik Boukhalfa (chafreaky), #890 (T21, T5, bank lift, owner bound and driver) and #795 (signed dual).\n- Hao Yan (@FanPUYen), #858 (T16 constructor, windows, independent checker).\n- #869/#870 U8 (NewBArch, ColdWitness/icekylinx).\n- Jeremy Kothe #799, Chafik Boukhalfa #741, and the PR589 bit supplier (DreamingOfClouds/eumemic lineage).\n- The PR514/484/507/635/645 controller lineage.\n- jon314159, #942: the same T37 construction and \u03ba, published first (independent, concurrent work).\n\n**Scope.** This is a finite conditional composition. All-size compiler, realization, hosting, precision/tape, analytic transfer and bit H1\u2013H5 remain inherited. The new explicit premise is the 1024-bit charged prefix.\n\nAI disclosure: prepared with Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic) via Claude Code, directed by Joel Pulikkan (GamingPuzzled). No independent human review is claimed.\n\n\ud83e\udd16 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
